# Public base URL. Used for canonical URLs, hreflang alternates, sitemap.xml,
# robots.txt and Open Graph image resolution. Must be the real origin in
# production or search engines will index localhost URLs.
#
# No sub-path any more: the app serves the domain root. If it is ever remounted
# under one (see NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH below), that path must be appended here
# too, or every canonical/sitemap URL points somewhere the app does not answer.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://davijara.uz

# Search-console ownership proofs. Both optional; unset = no verification <meta>
# is emitted (the local-dev default). Read at BUILD time, so setting one is a
# rebuild — deploy.sh exports them before `next build` like every NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# Give the TOKEN only, not the whole tag: the console shows a
#   <meta name="yandex-verification" content="abcd1234..." />
# and the value here is just `abcd1234...`.
#
# YANDEX_VERIFICATION first on purpose — Yandex carries a large share of search
# in Uzbekistan, so webmaster.yandex.ru is the registration that matters most.
# Then Google (search.google.com/search-console). Bing imports from Google.
# YANDEX_VERIFICATION=
# GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# Sub-path the app is served at. EMPTY means the domain root, which is both the
# production setup and what `npm run dev` does locally.
#
# It was "/site" until the site took over the root; davlat mulki monitoring now
# sits at /obyektlar instead. The mechanism is kept rather than deleted because
# the domain is still shared — /obyektlar, /kadastr, /api2, *.php and
# /api/search belong to other projects — so remounting has to stay possible.
#
# Feeds both `basePath` in next.config.ts and `withBasePath()` in
# src/lib/base-path.ts — the first covers Next's own assets and <Link>, the
# second covers raw <img src>/<form action>, which Next never rewrites. Must
# match the nginx `location` block in deploy/nginx-site-location.conf.
#
# Also feeds the admin session cookie's path (src/lib/auth/session.ts), which
# is pinned to `${BASE_PATH}/admin` so the token is never sent to the other
# projects sharing this domain.
#
# Baked into the client bundle at BUILD time, not read at runtime: changing it
# requires a rebuild, not just a service restart.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=

# Auction listings service — the FULL endpoint URL, not a base to append to.
# src/lib/data/listings.ts POSTs to it with HTTP Basic auth:
#
#   { "region": 1718, "adate": "2026-02-08", "bdate": "2026-08-07",
#     "lot_status": "active" }
#
# `region` is mandatory and takes one numeric id, so the national map is a
# fan-out over all fourteen. The ids are the standard SOATO region codes and
# live in src/content/regions.ts (`apiId`), each verified against the
# `summary.name` the service returns.
#
# Unset, or when every region fails, the site falls back to the verified
# records plus generated sample lots and shows a visible notice.
# LISTINGS_API_URL=http://host:port/api/rent-contracts/auction/list
# API_USER=
# API_PASSWORD=

# Speech — "Matnni o'qib berish" in the accessibility dialog.
#
# Azure AI Speech. Unset, and the feature reports itself unavailable: the
# player falls back to whatever voices the reader's own browser has — ru and
# en on a typical machine, never uz — and says so plainly on a page it cannot
# read. Nothing else on the site changes.
#
# Why a service is needed at all: no browser ships an Uzbek voice, and Google
# Cloud Text-to-Speech lists no uz-UZ either (measured 16.09.2026). Azure has
# uz-UZ-SardorNeural and uz-UZ-MadinaNeural, in the LATIN script this site is
# written in, plus ru-RU and en-US. ai.soliq.uz was evaluated and ruled out —
# see the note in src/lib/tts/provider.ts.
#
# REGION is the resource's region as it appears in the endpoint host, e.g.
# `uaenorth` or `westeurope`. ENDPOINT overrides the derived URL for a
# private-link, sovereign-cloud or gateway deployment.
#
# Billed per character — $15 per million, with 0,5 million a month free on the
# F0 tier, against a site whose whole readable text is about 95 000 characters
# in three languages. The audio is cached under DATA_DIR/tts, keyed by voice
# and text, so a paragraph is synthesised once and not once per reader, and
# /api/tts refuses to speak anything that is not written on the page it was
# given.
# Where the server reads its own pages back from, for /api/tts's check that a
# block of text is really on the page it claims to be.
#
# Loopback is tried first (both 127.0.0.1 and [::1], on PORT or 3000) and the
# public origin last: a server asking for https://davijara.uz from inside the
# network is refused, which is what made every synthesis answer
# `page-unavailable` in production.
#
# SET THIS WHENEVER THE PORT IS NOT IN `PORT`. On this site nginx proxies to
# http://[::1]:3001 and PM2 starts the app without PORT in the environment, so
# the guesses cannot find it:
# TTS_SELF_ORIGIN=http://[::1]:3001

# The warm-up's password. `npm run tts:warm` walks the sitemap and asks
# /api/tts/warm to speak every page, which fills the audio cache before the
# first reader arrives — Azure's free tier allows twenty calls a minute, and
# two readers at once are enough to reach it.
#
# Required by that route: with this unset the route refuses every caller, which
# is the right default for an endpoint that is a loop over a metered service.
# Generate one with `openssl rand -hex 24`.
# TTS_WARM_TOKEN=

# AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=
# AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=
# AZURE_SPEECH_ENDPOINT=

# Open bidding rooms — which lots are live (map pins, the "Jonli savdolar"
# tab and section, /joriy-savdolar, the menu entry).
#
# POST, no credentials: the public list behind e-auksion.uz's own "Lotlar →
# Joriy savdolar" page, asked for group 11 (state-property rent). NOT
# /api/front/lots/current — that homepage list carries no rent lots at all;
# see the comment in the module below.
#
# Only override this if the endpoint moves; the default below is what
# src/lib/data/live-auctions.ts uses. Our OWN listings feed cannot answer this
# question — a lot in its room right now still reports `lot_status:
# "Savdoda ishtirok etish uchun elektron arizalarni qabul qilish"`, the same
# value a lot whose auction is next week carries.
#
# Unreachable, and no lot is marked live: the map simply shows every pin in
# its ordinary navy.
# EAUKSION_CURLOTS_URL=https://e-auksion.uz/api/front/curlots?lang=uz

# Contracts register — the two middle hero cards.
#
# POST { region?: 1718, year: 2026 }, same Basic credentials as above.
# Returns `summary.contracts_count` and `summary.total_rental_area` (SQUARE
# METRES — the card divides by a million) plus a `data[]` row per district.
#
# Three things measured against the live service, not assumed:
#   * `region` is OPTIONAL here. Omit it for the republic; there is no
#     fan-out, unlike the listings endpoint.
#   * A DISTRICT code in `region` does not work — it answers "Ҳудуд топилмади"
#     with zeros. District figures come from the region call's `data[]`.
#   * `day` only moves the `daily_*` fields, so it is not sent.
#
# Unset or unreachable, the hero keeps the operator's verified static figures.
# RENT_CONTRACTS_API_URL=http://host:port/api/rent-contracts

# The same register's CONTRACT ROWS — /ijara-shartnomalari.
#
# POST { region: 1703, year: 2026 }, same Basic credentials. Defaults to
# RENT_CONTRACTS_API_URL + "/list-reg", so it only needs setting if the
# service moves it. `region` is REQUIRED here (the republic is 14 calls).
# RENT_CONTRACTS_LIST_URL=http://host:port/api/rent-contracts/list-reg

# Cadastre gateway — building names and addresses for /ijara-shartnomalari.
#
# GET <url>?tin=<holder STIR>&cad_number=<number>, HTTP Basic. `tin` must be
# the STIR of the organisation that HOLDS the building — any other answers
# 2108 "tashkilotga tegishli emas". The contracts register sends no TIN yet,
# so until it does, names come from the older service below instead.
# CADDATA_BASE_URL=http://host:port/markaz/cad_data
# CADDATA_USERNAME=
# CADDATA_PASSWORD=

# The nightly name warm-up — /api/cadastre/warm and scripts/warm-cadastre.mjs
# (cron line in DEPLOY.md). Without it the route refuses every caller.
# Generate one with `openssl rand -hex 24`.
# CADASTRE_WARM_TOKEN=

# Older cadastre service — the fallback for objects with no holder TIN.
#
# GET <url>?token=<token>&num=14:12:05:01:05:0048, one request per number.
# Answers are kept in the database (cadastre_objects), so each number is
# asked about once. Without these two the page still works and shows the
# cadastre number where the name would be. The token is a secret: write it
# here, on the server, never in chat or in git. The response also carries
# the owners' passport/PINFL — the code reads only name and address.
# CADASTRE_API_URL=http://otchet.davbaho.uz/api/get_cadastre_info/1
# CADASTRE_API_TOKEN=

# Order endpoint — the ONLY source of lot photographs.
#
# The listings endpoint above returns no image reference, and the URLs on
# media.e-auksion.uz are opaque content hashes that cannot be derived from a
# lot number, so a photo has to be looked up per lot. This endpoint does that,
# one order at a time:
#
#   POST { "order": 1728631, "username": …, "password": …, "language": "uz" }
#   -> { result_code: 0, orders: [ { images: [ { image, is_main } … ] } ] }
#
# Because it is one request per lot and the map carries ~1,150 pins, images are
# fetched lazily — only for lots actually on screen. See lib/data/lot-images.ts.
#
# NOTE THE `/ws/` SEGMENT — it is not optional and not guessable. Without it
# the host answers an immediate nginx 404; nine other path spellings were tried
# against it before the right one was confirmed.
# ORDER_API_URL=http://host:port/ws/api/services/common/get-order

# CREDENTIALS ARE PER REGION, and this is the part that silently half-works if
# it is skipped. Each of the fourteen territorial offices has its own account
# on this service, and the username and password are both that office's INN.
# Credentials go in the request BODY here, not as HTTP Basic.
#
# A lot requested with ANOTHER region's account does not error — it comes back
# with no images. So a single shared account makes exactly one region show
# photographs while the other thirteen show placeholders, which reads as a bug
# in the site rather than as missing configuration.
#
# Keyed by the SOATO region id in src/content/regions.ts, so every line can be
# checked against that table.
#
# ⚠ NEVER PUT A COMMENT ON THE SAME LINE AS A VALUE.
#
#     ORDER_API_INN_1727=300393445   # Toshkent viloyati   ← BROKEN
#
# systemd's EnvironmentFile= does not strip trailing `#` comments: the value
# becomes the literal string "300393445   # Toshkent viloyati" and the service
# rejects it with `result_code 25: Foydalanuvchi aniqlanmadi`. It is nastier
# than it looks because `dotenv` — which the BUILD step uses — does strip them,
# so the same file works locally and fails in production. Done for real; this
# template used to invite it. The region name goes ABOVE its line:
#
# Toshkent shahri
# ORDER_API_INN_1726=
# Toshkent viloyati
# ORDER_API_INN_1727=
# Samarqand
# ORDER_API_INN_1718=
# Buxoro
# ORDER_API_INN_1706=
# Xorazm
# ORDER_API_INN_1733=
# Farg'ona
# ORDER_API_INN_1730=
# Andijon
# ORDER_API_INN_1703=
# Namangan
# ORDER_API_INN_1714=
# Qashqadaryo
# ORDER_API_INN_1710=
# Surxondaryo
# ORDER_API_INN_1722=
# Jizzax
# ORDER_API_INN_1708=
# Sirdaryo
# ORDER_API_INN_1724=
# Navoiy
# ORDER_API_INN_1712=
# Qoraqalpog'iston
# ORDER_API_INN_1735=
#
# Fallback for any region with no line above, so a partly-filled config still
# serves the regions it does cover.
# ORDER_API_USER=
# ORDER_API_PASSWORD=

# Basemap tiles for both Leaflet maps (the catalogue's and /aloqa's).
#
# UNSET BY DESIGN — defaults to OpenStreetMap's own tile server, at the
# operator's choice. CARTO's Voyager basemap (the original choice) now stamps
# every tile "API KEY REQUIRED" for unauthenticated requests; Wikimedia's tile
# service is flatly restricted to Wikimedia's own sites. OSM's own server does
# NOT require prior arrangement for a normal website — a browser loading
# tiles via a plain <img>, which is what Leaflet does, already satisfies its
# policy. What it does not offer is any SLA: OSMF's own policy states they
# "may block access, without notice, if your usage degrades the service."
# Full account, including what happened when this was evaluated, in
# src/lib/map-tiles.ts — read it before changing this default.
#
# TO SWITCH TO A KEYED PROVIDER instead (MapTiler, Stadia Maps, CARTO with an
# account this time — worth doing if OSM's best-effort availability ever
# becomes a problem in practice), set BOTH and rebuild. Get the exact URL
# template and attribution HTML from the provider's own dashboard, not by
# guessing at the pattern — that is exactly what went wrong with CARTO's
# anonymous CDN here:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILE_URL=https://provider.example/{z}/{x}/{y}.png?key=…
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILE_ATTRIBUTION=&copy; <a href="https://provider.example">Provider</a>
#
# Also add that host to the CSP `img-src` in next.config.ts, or the browser
# blocks the new tiles even after this env var and Next both allow them.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is required, not optional: Leaflet's <TileLayer> runs in the
# browser, so the value has to be in the client bundle — see the note in
# map-tiles.ts for why a tile key is fine to expose that way. Both are baked
# in at BUILD time, like every NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable; changing either needs a
# rebuild, not just a service restart.
#
# NOTE: do not restore the legacy configuration, which scraped Google Maps
# tiles from {s}.google.com/vt/ in breach of their terms of service.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILE_ATTRIBUTION=

# Yandex.Metrica counter id — the operator's analytics panel.
#
# UNSET BY DEFAULT, and that is the whole of local development: nothing loads,
# no cookie is set, and the CSP in next.config.ts stays as tight as its comment
# claims. Set it here and the site loads the Metrica tag and the policy widens
# to allow exactly one third-party origin (mc.yandex.ru).
#
# The 8-digit number from mc.yandex.ru/metrika, digits only:
#   YANDEX_METRICA_ID=98765432
#
# NOT NEXT_PUBLIC_: the id is written into the inline snippet on the server, so
# the browser never reads it from process.env. Still a BUILD-time value though
# — deploy.sh exports every var in this file before `next build`, and both the
# CSP header and the <YandexMetrica> component read it then. Changing it is a
# rebuild, not just a service restart.
#
# Session recording (Webvisor) is OFF in src/components/layout/yandex-metrica.tsx
# on purpose — recording a citizen's every move on a state portal is not a
# default. Turn it on from the Metrica dashboard if it is wanted; a code-side
# webvisor would also need the CSP widened (see the note in next.config.ts).
# YANDEX_METRICA_ID=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Boshqaruv paneli — ADMIN PANEL
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# WHERE THE DATABASE AND UPLOADS LIVE.
#
# ⚠ This MUST point outside the release directory. deploy.sh builds each
# release into `releases/<timestamp>/` and keeps only the last five — anything
# written inside a release is deleted five deploys later, silently, taking
# every news item and uploaded image with it. `shared/` is the directory that
# survives deploys; it is already where .env itself is kept, for this reason.
#
# In production:
#   DATA_DIR=/var/www/davijara/shared/data
#
# Left unset, the app falls back to `.data/` beside the source tree, which is
# gitignored and correct for local development only.
#
# The directory is created on first use. It holds:
#   davijara.db          the SQLite database (plus -wal and -shm alongside it)
#   uploads/             images and files added by editors
#
# BACKUP: stop nothing, copy nothing by hand mid-write. Use SQLite's own
# consistent snapshot, which is safe while the site is running:
#   sqlite3 /var/www/davijara/shared/data/davijara.db ".backup '/backup/davijara-$(date +%F).db'"
# and back up the uploads/ directory with it — the database stores file names,
# not file contents, so one without the other restores to broken images.
# DATA_DIR=

# Full path to the database file. Only needed to put it somewhere other than
# DATA_DIR/davijara.db — a separate disk, for instance. Overrides DATA_DIR.
# DATABASE_PATH=

# FIRST-RUN SETUP KEY.
#
# /admin/setup creates the first administrator and then closes permanently.
# That page asks for this value, so that only someone who can read this file
# on the server can complete setup — without it, whoever reaches the URL first
# after a deploy becomes the administrator of a state portal.
#
# Generate a fresh one, never reuse an example:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# After the first administrator exists this value is no longer used by
# anything and SHOULD BE DELETED from this file.
# ADMIN_SETUP_TOKEN=
